<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Novae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Novae was a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress and town on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near modern Svishtov in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Founded in the 1st century CE, it was long the base of the First Italian Legion and part of the Danube frontier of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a>. In late antiquity it became a fortified town with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>, and the Ostrogothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a> used it as his base in the 480s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/novae.jpg" alt="Novae" width="250" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA/CXC/M.Weiss · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Making_a_Nova.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
